; S1a.3.1 — an unbound relation head in a `:match` premise.
;
; `?R` is not a parameter, so the activator cannot bind it, and M1 matches
; relations per activator (Q29). Until S1.22.0 `_compile_relation` returned
; `[]` here — dropping the premise. The plan's only premise gone, `steps` is
; empty, and the matcher reads an empty step tuple as one VACUOUS match, so
; the rule fired unconditionally and stored its conclusion.
(relation p Thing)

(rule uses-free-head (?S)
  :match  (?R ?x)
  :assert (p ?x))

(uses-free-head p)
